# This is a proposal for how you write dialogue. Nothing reads it yet.
# You write these in TextEdit. No programming, no Godot. One file per scene.
#
#   #  a line starting with hash is a note to yourself, ignored by the game
#   ::  starts a new chunk the game can jump to
#   NAME:  who is speaking
#   (something in brackets) is a stage direction for the actor and for me
#   >  a choice the player can tap
#   ->  jump to another chunk
#   @  an instruction to me (play a sound, move the camera, give her a skill)

:: start
# Prologue. 2026, the trench, first light. Eva is filming on her phone.
EVA: (to her phone, low) Day nineteen. Sun's not up, Ishita's not up, and I am
EVA: standing in a hole my mother was laughed out of a conference for pointing at.
@ objective "Clear the trench floor"
@ skill_unlock excavation
-> ishita_arrives

:: ishita_arrives
ISHITA: (off, above) You're talking to your phone again.
EVA: I'm talking to two million people. You're the one talking to nobody.
> "Come down and look at this."     -> show_her
> (say nothing, keep digging)        -> keep_digging

:: show_her
ISHITA: (sliding down into the trench) ...That's not backfill.
EVA: No. That's a lintel.
@ camera look_at sealed_door
-> the_door

:: keep_digging
EVA: (to herself) Suit yourself.
-> the_door

:: the_door
# The beat the whole prologue exists for.
@ music swell_discovery
EVA: (quiet, not performing any more) Mum was right.
-> END
